+A CORRECT implementation that is mechanically DIFFERENT from the Triton oracle: it
+computes the combined log-normalizer with ``torch.logsumexp`` over the chunk axis and
+contracts the softmax-weighted partials with ``torch.einsum`` (no explicit max /
+manual denominator / materialized (N, R, D) product like the naive baseline, and no
+hand-written kernel like the oracle), then hands the whole core to ``torch.compile`` so
+the Inductor backend fuses it into a small number of generated kernels — a different
+codegen path from the oracle. Validation runs eagerly (so the TypeError / ValueError
+error-contract raises before any compiled region). It must earn a POSITIVE reward on
+its own merit; if the verifier could only reward the exact oracle code it would be
+oracle-overfit and must be fixed. Reviewer-only; NEVER baked into the image.
 """
 
